Subject: [PATCH 01/19] fix(eval): correct benchmark parquet paths and retarget
 GPU budget to 4x A6000

The BENCHMARKS array pointed at a dataset layout that no longer exists on
HF (siyich/spacetools-eval-benchmarks was reorganized to a flat data/
directory), so run_eval.sh aborted at the "Missing: ..." precheck before
starting Toolshed. Benchmark keys already map 1:1 to the parquet
filenames, so the array is replaced wholesale.

Also retarget the GPU budget from the upstream 8-GPU training assumption
to a 4x A6000 eval node: NUM_GPUS 8->4, EVAL_GPUS 4->2 (two data-parallel
sglang replicas for the 3B policy at tensor_model_parallel_size=1), and
trim the tool actors' Ray fractions from 2.3 to 1.9 so policy (2.0) plus
tools fits in 4.0. Fractions are scheduling units, not memory caps; the
trim keeps every num_actors at the upstream default of 2, avoiding a
second deviation from the paper's configuration.

Applied to both the v1 and v2 tool blocks to keep them consistent.
---
 examples/toolshed/run_eval.sh | 42 +++++++++++++++++------------------
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)

diff --git a/examples/toolshed/run_eval.sh b/examples/toolshed/run_eval.sh
index ce9dafaf..5024d05f 100755
--- a/examples/toolshed/run_eval.sh
+++ b/examples/toolshed/run_eval.sh
@@ -23,8 +23,8 @@
